    "case_id": "303",
    "case_summary": "A female infant with history of acute lymphoblastic leukemia was admitted for reinduction chemotherapy. Seventeen days after her last day of chemotherapy, while neutropenic, she became febrile. Patient had an indwelling catheter.\n\nSeveral vesicles with an erythematous base were observed on the lower back and left thigh.\n\n- Tissue and blood cultures were obtained- Punch biopsy of vesicle on lower back was performed- Microscopic examination:  * Hematoxylin-eosin stain showed focal epidermal and subepidermal necrosis with numerous filamentous bacilli with septa  * Gram stain revealed numerous gram-variable rods in the necrotic epidermis and dermis  * Periodic acid-Schiff staining was negative for fungal elements- PCR testing for herpes simplex virus (HSV) and varicella zoster virus (VZV) were negative- CT scan with contrast of thorax and brain showed lesions in the liver and brain- Images:  Image A Title: Clinical presentation  Image A Description: Scattered vesicles with an erythematous base on the lower back  Image B Title: Histopathology (H&E, ×200)  Image C Title: Histopathology (H&E, ×600)  Image D Title: Gram stain (×600)",
    "frontier": [
      "B1",
      "B2",
      "B3",
      "B4"
    ],
